gal","vintage":"legal"},"cmc":3.0},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["W"],"colors":["W"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{W}","name":"Cloudshift","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","oracle_text":"Exile target creature you control, then return that card to the battlefield under your control.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2025-11-21","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":4.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"commander":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}","name":"Icy Manipulator","oracle_id":"3608f1f7-8dc5-4dd1-ae91-c830e1de9529","oracle_text":"{1}, {T}: Tap target artifact, creature, or land.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2023-01-13","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If Rest in Peace is destroyed by a spell, Rest in Peace will be exiled and then the spell will be put into its owner's graveyard.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card is discarded while Rest in Peace is on the battlefield, abilities that function when a card is discarded (such as madness) still work, even though that card never reaches a graveyard. In addition, spells or abilities that check the characteristics of a discarded card (such as Chandra Ablaze's first ability) can find that card in exile.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While Rest in Peace is on the battlefield, abilities that trigger whenever a creature dies won't trigger because cards and tokens are never put into a player's graveyard.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"As Victimize resolves, you must sacrifice a creature if able. You can't change your mind and choose not to sacrifice anything.","oracle_id":"240e85d3-e495-4877-8609-4b4056c402f7","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If one of the targeted creature cards is an illegal target (for instance, because it has left your graveyard before Victimize resolves), you'll still sacrifice a creature and put the other card onto the battlefield. If both are illegal targets, Victimize won't resolve. You won't sacrifice a creature.","oracle_id":"240e85d3-e495-4877-8609-4b4056c402f7","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The creature you sacrifice isn't chosen until Victimize resolves. You can't return the creature you sacrifice because it will still be on the battlefield at the time targets are chosen.","oracle_id":"240e85d3-e495-4877-8609-4b4056c402f7","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You must choose two targets. You can't cast Victimize targeting only one creature card.","oracle_id":"240e85d3-e495-4877-8609-4b4056c402f7","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"It doesn’t matter who controlled the artifact while it was on the battlefield, only whose graveyard it was put into.","oracle_id":"c24b0c7d-1a4b-4eca-8d83-9e81ed3b3b27","published_at":"2011-01-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the target card is no longer in the graveyard when Cremate tries to resolve, it won't resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won't draw a card.","oracle_id":"c6a2e410-b182-48d1-aeb2-bc8de27e9cd2","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You must be able to target a card in a graveyard to cast Cremate.","oracle_id":"c6a2e410-b182-48d1-aeb2-bc8de27e9cd2","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"oracle_id":"dba16032-66c1-4ccb-9d65-d41ac550d182","published_at":"2010-03-01","source":"wotc","comment":"For Amulet of Vigor's ability to trigger, a permanent must enter tapped due to an effect that says \"put [the permanent] onto the battlefield tapped,\" \"[this permanent] enters tapped,\" or the like. If it enters untapped, the ability won't trigger, even if you tap that permanent afterward."},{"oracle_id":"dba16032-66c1-4ccb-9d65-d41ac550d182","published_at":"2010-03-01","source":"wotc","comment":"If you control more than one Amulet of Vigor, each Amulet's ability triggers when a permanent enters tapped and under your control. The first ability that resolves will untap that permanent. If the permanent somehow becomes tapped again before the next ability resolves, the next ability will untap it as well (and so on)."}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
